## 5. No SERVICE_PENDING names, no protocol rows, no hot file beyond the three above: the modules register no service.

## 6. Seams for the tasks that use this layer (nothing else to wire now)
- `oplist::get_operator_list(&Document, &Page, Option<&dyn FontProvider>) -> Result<OperatorList>` is `page.getOperatorList()` of the display layer
  (the `oplist` intent: pdf.js builds that list without its queue optimizer, so repeated images and `q cm path Q` runs are NOT folded; this was
  recorded from pdf.js 6.4 and is what pdf-analysis.mjs reads). `OperatorList::with_transforms()` is the analysis's `applyGraphicsOp` walk
  (the transform in force at every operator); `PathData::subpaths()` is its `pathSubpaths`.
- FONT OBJECT SEAM (owner: nr-exthost-pdf-font-object, whose files are still placeholders in this tree): the evaluator takes the font object through
  `oplist::FontProvider::translate_font(&Arc<Dict>, &Xref) -> Result<Arc<dyn FontObject>>` and `FontObject::{is_type3, chars_to_glyphs, bbox}`.
  The font-object task implements both traits over its `Font` and passes the provider to `get_operator_list`. Without a provider every font reads as
  unavailable (pdf.js `ErrorFont`: a shown string has no glyphs) and the pass reports that once at error level. The Type3 glyph procedures
  (`loadType3Data`: one operator list per CharProcs entry, colour operators of `d1` glyphs removed, glyph boxes joined) are read by this task
  once the provider says a font is Type3 (`LoadedFont::type3`).
- `outline_read::get_page_index(&Document, Ref)` is `Catalog.getPageIndex`; `get_destination(&Document, &str)` is `Catalog.getDestination`;
  `get_outline(&Document)` is `Catalog.documentOutline`; `parse_dest_dictionary` is `Catalog.parseDestDictionary` (the outline items and the link
  annotations share it). The links of `annotations::get_annotations` are in page order, widgets then popups last, as pdf.js sorts them.

## 7. Verify (after 1 to 3)
cargo nextest run -p mixdog-pdf --offline
cargo clippy -p mixdog-pdf --all-targets --offline -- -D warnings
The ignored `twin_live_oplist` re-records with Node (`node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-oplist.mjs --tree <tree>`).
The replay test `operator_lists_annotations_and_outline_equal_pdfjs` compares exactly (every number as a double) and prints the first differences per
document: a difference there is a port defect to fix in the module it names (ops: oplist; annots: annotations; outline/dests: outline_read).
